# WordBuddy intentionally does not read provider credentials from .env files.
# Configure API keys in Settings so they are stored by the native secret store.
#
# To force correctness-only behavior, set WB_DISABLE_LLM=1 in the shell that
# launches WordBuddy. A .env file is not loaded into the Rust process:
#
# PowerShell: $env:WB_DISABLE_LLM = "1"
# bash/zsh:   export WB_DISABLE_LLM=1
